Privacy Policy for UTM Forge
Effective date: March 24, 2026

Overview
UTM Forge is a Chrome extension that helps users build and manage UTM tracking URLs. This privacy policy explains what data the extension handles and how it is used.

Data Collection
UTM Forge does not collect, transmit, or store any personal data on external servers. The extension has no backend, no analytics, and no account system.

Data Storage
All data generated by UTM Forge — including saved URLs, history, and favorites — is stored exclusively on your local device using Chrome's built-in chrome.storage.local API. This data never leaves your browser and is not accessible to the developer or any third party.

Permissions
UTM Forge requests the following browser permissions:

storage — to save your UTM history and favorites locally on your device
contextMenus — to add a right-click menu option for applying UTM parameters to selected URLs
scripting — to paste the generated UTM URL into the active page when selected from the right-click menu
notifications — to confirm when a UTM URL has been successfully applied
host_permissions (all URLs) — required to inject the paste script on any webpage where you use the right-click feature

None of these permissions are used to collect or transmit data.

Third-Party Services
UTM Forge does not integrate with or transmit data to any third-party services.

Changes to This Policy
If this policy changes in a future version of the extension, the updated policy will be posted at this URL with a revised effective date.

Contact
If you have any questions about this privacy policy, please open an issue on the GitHub repository.
